# Per-sleeve kill-switch — the SINGLE source of truth for which strategy sleeves run.
#
# Flip a sleeve to "off" and redeploy to retire it. Unlike `systemctl disable` by hand
# (which the next deploy silently re-enables), this SURVIVES deploys: the deploy enables
# only the "on" sleeves and `disable --now`s the "off" ones, and the verify + the liveness
# watchdog stop expecting them.
#
# SAFETY — what "off" does and does NOT do:
#   * "off" stops the sleeve's daemon -> NO NEW entries.
#   * It does NOT flatten open positions. Each open position keeps its Bybit-managed
#     server-side disaster stop AND ws_risk protection (the risk service always runs and
#     keeps reading every configured ledger root), so positions exit naturally with no
#     orphan/flatten risk. Wind a sleeve to flat BEFORE you consider it fully retired.
#   * The short sleeve's root is ws_risk's primary; turning SHORT off stops its entry
#     daemon but ws_risk still uses that root. The risk service itself has no toggle.
#
# Accepted values: on | off  (also 1/true/yes == on). Override per host in
# /etc/liquidity-migration/sleeves.env (sourced/loaded AFTER this file, so it wins).
#
# Plain KEY=value (no shell ${:-} expansion) so this file is valid as BOTH a bash `source`
# (deploy/verify) AND a systemd EnvironmentFile (the liveness watchdog reads the toggles to
# skip an intentionally-off sleeve). Keep it that way.

# SHORT  = liquidity-migration short (event_demo): the demo entry daemon — the REAL forward demo.
# 2026-06-09 operator instruction: VPS runs ONLY the continuous system (demo+paper).
SHORT_SLEEVE=off
# SHORT_PAPER = the short sleeve's PAPER shadow (a no-order dry-run on its own ledger root; the
# daily paper<->demo reconcile arbiter). Split out of SHORT_SLEEVE so a small/low-RAM host can run
# the demo WITHOUT this second full-universe paper process. ON 2026-06-04: short demo measured at
# only ~535 MB on the 4 GB box, leaving headroom, so the reconcile shadow is back. Flip to off to
# shed it first if the box gets memory-tight.
# RE-ENABLED 2026-06-11 (operator "fix the stale continuous-vs-daily forward"): the
# comparator's DAILY leg reads this sleeve's event_demo_trades ledger; with it off the
# comparison is structurally starved (common_days stuck 1/30, lagging=daily, can never
# mature). Paper submits NO orders, so the 2026-06-09 "only continuous trades"
# instruction stands. The 30-common-day clock starts ticking at the next deploy.
SHORT_PAPER_SLEEVE=on
# LONG   = long-native v11a: demo + paper services (a diversifier overlay). FORWARD-DEMO STARTED
# 2026-06-04 on this box (first time). "on" shares the one netted demo account's margin with short
# (no budget throttle, so sleeves compete for demo equity). Flip to off to retire it; open demo
# positions then ride to natural exit under the always-on risk service (no flatten).
LONG_SLEEVE=off
# CONTINUOUS = continuous-fade DEMO order-submitting sleeve.
# ON 2026-06-09 by EXPLICIT operator instruction: the rebuilt box runs ONLY the
# continuous system (demo orders + paper shadow) to accumulate forward evidence and
# observed-fill cost calibration. Demo account only (REAL_MONEY=false). Honest status:
# continuous remains research-stage, NOT promoted; the rmom latency knife-edge caveat
# (STATE.md Methodology Debts) stands; demo fills are execution evidence, not alpha
# proof. The rmom panel is the post-look-ahead-fix shift3 causal build.
CONTINUOUS_SLEEVE=on
# CONTINUOUS_PAPER = no-order continuous_rebalance_v1 evidence collector. This can run
# while CONTINUOUS_SLEEVE stays off: SUBMIT_ORDERS=0, RECORD_DRY_RUN=1, PAPER_MODE=1.
# It feeds the continuous-vs-daily forward comparator without touching the demo account.
CONTINUOUS_PAPER_SLEEVE=on
